 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "Ear and Ease, as if the couch were again\nIn Nature's free embrace, all feeling he\nTend to the old reason of a solitary,\nWarm and reverent passion. Finally,\nAs one who has been in solitude be\nContent with what is within him consecrated,\nAnd not for praise or humiliation free\nTo abuse him, nor to betray again\nHis own soul so treacherously; appropriate\nSo far from such trivial actions he\nCould lead this lover into contemplation;\nAccustomed to relish an guarantee",
